{"Non-atomic retry increment: retryCount is updated using a read-then-write (retryCount: reminder.retryCount + 1), which can lose increments if two cron executions update the same reminder between read and write": 0.6142109632492065, "Unscoped deletion deletes non-SMS reminders: The deleteMany OR condition's second branch { retryCount: { gt: 1 } } lacks a method: WorkflowMethods.SMS filter, so the SMS cron job will delete ALL WorkflowReminder records with retryCount > 1 regardless of method type (EMAIL, WHATSAPP)": 0.9961951971054077, "Unguarded update in catch block: The catch block awaits prisma.workflowReminder.update without handling failures; if the reminder is missing (e.g., deleted concurrently) the update can throw and abort processing subsequent reminders": 0.9544582962989807, "No retry increment for invalid data: When message is empty/null or sendTo is falsy, the code falls through without incrementing retryCount, so reminders with permanently invalid data remain at retryCount: 0 and scheduled: false, causing them to be re-fetched and wastefully re-processed on every cron run": 0.9157000184059143}